PhpDoc
******

.[perex]
The `phpdoc` section decides on doc comments (`/** */`): what should not be in them (annotations like `@author`, an annotation that only repeats the native type, an empty comment), how types are written in them, when a property comment fits on one line, and what in them is most likely a mistake.

PHPStan and your editor both read doc comments, so their content matters more than the content of an ordinary comment. The keys `forbiddenAnnotations` and `forbiddenLines` remove what the project does not want in comments, `annotation.nativeTypeOnly` removes an annotation that only repeats the native type of the signature, and the keys under `types` unify how types are written. A comment that is left empty after these removals disappears completely. Other keys under `annotation`, such as `extraParam`, `duplicateReturn`, `duplicateVar` and `empty`, report what contradicts the signature or the comment itself: a `@param` for a parameter that does not exist, a second `@return`, or an annotation with no content.

```neon
phpdoc:
	forbiddenAnnotations: ['@author']
	empty: forbidden
	annotation:
		nativeTypeOnly: forbidden
	property:
		lineSpan: collapsed
	types:
		builtin: canonical
```

```php .[before]
class Cart
{
	/**
	 * @author John
	 * @var integer[]
	 */
	private array $items = [];  // Annotation `@author` is forbidden. // The doc comment with a single annotation must be written on one line. // The type `integer` in a doc comment must be written `int`.

	/**
	 * @param string $name
	 * @return void
	 */
	public function add(string $name): void  // Useless `@param` annotation for the parameter `$name`, because the native type says the same. // Useless `@return` annotation, because the native return type says the same.
	{
	}
}
```

```php .[after]
class Cart
{
	/** @var int[] */
	private array $items = [];

	public function add(string $name): void
	{
	}
}
```

The [types |types] section decides on the types that the code itself declares. A class name mentioned in a comment always keeps its import in use, so cleaning up the imports does not remove that import.


phpdoc.empty
============

An empty doc comment, which is removed.

- `forbidden`: never there
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `forbidden`, symfony `forbidden`, laravel `forbidden` · covers `no_empty_phpdoc` .[decision-facts]


phpdoc.annotation.casing
========================

The letter case of a known annotation.

- `canonical`: as it is known, `@inheritDoc`, `@phpstan-var`
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `canonical`, symfony `keep`, laravel `keep` · covers `phpdoc_tag_casing`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.Commenting.AnnotationName` .[decision-facts]


phpdoc.annotation.inlineVar
===========================

An inline `@var` says what `assert($x instanceof Foo)` checks.

- `forbidden`: never there
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `forbidden`, symfony `keep`, laravel `keep` · covers `SlevomatCodingStandard.PHP.RequireExplicitAssertion` .[decision-facts]


phpdoc.forbiddenAnnotations
===========================

The annotations removed from doc comments, written with the `@`, such as `@author` and `@package`.

- a list of names
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `[@access, @author, @copyright, @created, @license, @package, @since, @subpackage, @todo, @version]`, symfony `keep`, laravel `[@access, @package, @subpackage]` · covers `general_phpdoc_annotation_remove`, `phpdoc_no_access`, `phpdoc_no_package`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.Commenting.ForbiddenAnnotations` .[decision-facts]


phpdoc.forbiddenLines
=====================

The patterns of the lines of a description removed from doc comments, such as `~^Created by \S+\.\z~i`, what a pattern matches going and the line with it where nothing else is left.

- a list of regular expressions
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `['~^(?:(?!private|protected|static)\S+ )?(?:con|de)structor\.\z~i', '~^\S+ [gs]etter\.\z~i']`, symfony `keep`, laravel `keep` · covers `SlevomatCodingStandard.Commenting.ForbiddenComments` .[decision-facts]


phpdoc.annotation.extraParam
============================

A `@param` naming a parameter the function does not have.

- `forbidden`: never there
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `forbidden`, symfony `keep`, laravel `keep` · covers `Squiz.Commenting.FunctionComment.ExtraParamComment` .[decision-facts]


phpdoc.annotation.duplicateParam
================================

A second `@param` of one parameter.

- `forbidden`: never there
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `forbidden`, symfony `keep`, laravel `keep` .[decision-facts]


phpdoc.annotation.duplicateReturn
=================================

A second `@return` of a function.

- `forbidden`: never there
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `forbidden`, symfony `keep`, laravel `keep` · covers `Squiz.Commenting.FunctionComment.DuplicateReturn` .[decision-facts]


phpdoc.annotation.duplicateVar
==============================

A second `@var` of a property.

- `forbidden`: never there
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `forbidden`, symfony `keep`, laravel `keep` · covers `Squiz.Commenting.VariableComment` .[decision-facts]


phpdoc.annotation.empty
=======================

A `@param`, `@return`, `@var` or `@see` without content.

- `forbidden`: never there
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `forbidden`, symfony `keep`, laravel `keep` · covers `Squiz.Commenting.VariableComment` .[decision-facts]


phpdoc.annotation.plainComment
==============================

An annotation in a plain comment, `/* @var */` or `/**@var` without the blank, where a doc comment means it: any annotation above a declaration, an inline `@var` above another statement.

- `forbidden`: never there
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `forbidden`, symfony `keep`, laravel `keep` · covers `SlevomatCodingStandard.Commenting.InlineDocCommentDeclaration.InvalidCommentType` .[decision-facts]


phpdoc.property.plainComment
============================

A plain comment describing a property, `//` or `/* */` where `/** */` belongs, reported.

- `forbidden`: never there
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `forbidden`, symfony `keep`, laravel `keep` · covers `Squiz.Commenting.VariableComment` .[decision-facts]


phpdoc.aboveAttributes
======================

The doc comment stands above the attributes.

- `required`: always there
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `required`, psr12 `keep`, nette `required`, symfony `keep`, laravel `keep` · covers `SlevomatCodingStandard.Attributes.RequireAttributeAfterDocComment` .[decision-facts]


phpdoc.stars
============

The `*` opening each line of a doc comment.

- `aligned`: each `*` below the first `*` of the opening `/**`
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `aligned`, symfony `keep`, laravel `aligned` · covers `align_multiline_comment`, `phpdoc_indent`, `Squiz.Commenting.DocCommentAlignment` .[decision-facts]


phpdoc.blankLines
=================

The blank lines inside a doc comment.

- `trimmed`: none at the start or the end, at most one in a row inside
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `trimmed`, symfony `trimmed`, laravel `trimmed` · covers `phpdoc_trim`, `phpdoc_trim_consecutive_blank_line_separation` .[decision-facts]


phpdoc.types.builtin
====================

How a built-in type in a doc comment is written, `int` and never `integer` or `Int`.

- `canonical`: the short lowercase name of a built-in type, `never` for `no-return`
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `canonical`, symfony `canonical`, laravel `canonical` · covers `PhpCsFixerCustomFixers/phpdoc_type_list`, `phpdoc_list_type`, `phpdoc_scalar`, `phpdoc_types`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.TypeHints.LongTypeHints` .[decision-facts]


phpdoc.types.duplicate
======================

A type a union of a doc comment names twice, `int|integer`.

- `forbidden`: never there
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `forbidden`, symfony `forbidden`, laravel `keep` · covers `phpdoc_no_duplicate_types`, `phpdoc_types_no_duplicates` .[decision-facts]


phpdoc.types.nullable
=====================

How a type of a doc comment of one type and `null` is written.

- `'?T'`: a single type with `null` written with `?`
- `'T|null'`: a union with `null`, which `phpdoc.types.nullPosition` places
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `keep`, symfony `keep`, laravel `keep` .[decision-facts]


phpdoc.types.nullPosition
=========================

Where `null` stands in a union type of a doc comment.

- `last`: `int|string|null`
- `first`: `null|int|string`
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `last`, symfony `last`, laravel `keep` · covers `phpdoc_types_order`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.TypeHints.NullTypeHintOnLastPosition` .[decision-facts]


phpdoc.types.unionOrder
=======================

The order of the types of a union type of a doc comment.

- `alphabetical`: the types beside `null` sorted by name, case-insensitively
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `keep`, symfony `keep`, laravel `keep` · covers `phpdoc_types_order` .[decision-facts]


phpdoc.types.array
==================

How an array type of a doc comment is written; `list<T>` is a different type and stays.

- `'array<T>'`: the generic notation
- `'T[]'`: the brackets
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `keep`, symfony `keep`, laravel `keep` · covers `PhpCsFixerCustomFixers/phpdoc_array_style`, `PhpCsFixerCustomFixers/phpdoc_type_list`, `phpdoc_array_type`, `phpdoc_list_type`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.TypeHints.DisallowArrayTypeHintSyntax` .[decision-facts]


phpdoc.property.promoted
========================

The annotation of a promoted property.

- `'@var'`: a `@var` at the property, not a `@param` of the constructor
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `@var`, symfony `keep`, laravel `keep` .[decision-facts]


phpdoc.property.lineSpan
========================

A property doc comment with a single annotation and no description.

- `collapsed`: on one line, `/** @var int */`
- `expanded`: over three lines, the annotation on the one in the middle
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `collapsed`, symfony `keep`, laravel `keep` · covers `phpdoc_line_span`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.Commenting.DisallowOneLinePropertyDocComment`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.Commenting.RequireOneLinePropertyDocComment` .[decision-facts]


phpdoc.annotation.constantVar
=============================

A `@var` on a class constant that says nothing.

- `forbidden`: never there
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `forbidden`, symfony `keep`, laravel `keep` · covers `SlevomatCodingStandard.TypeHints.UselessConstantTypeHint` .[decision-facts]


phpdoc.inheritdocOnly
=====================

A doc comment of `@inheritDoc` alone.

- `forbidden`: never there
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `forbidden`, symfony `keep`, laravel `keep` · covers `phpdoc_no_useless_inheritdoc`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.Commenting.UselessInheritDocComment` .[decision-facts]


phpdoc.annotation.itemTypes
===========================

An array, iterable or traversable declaration has an annotation saying what its items are, reported.

- `required`: always there
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `keep`, symfony `keep`, laravel `keep` · covers `SlevomatCodingStandard.TypeHints.ParameterTypeHint`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.TypeHints.PropertyTypeHint`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.TypeHints.ReturnTypeHint` .[decision-facts]


phpdoc.annotation.nativeTypeOnly
================================

A `@param`, `@return` or `@var` without a description that says only the native type.

- `forbidden`: never there
- `keep`: nothing is enforced, the code stays as it is

Default `keep` · standards: perCs `keep`, psr12 `keep`, nette `forbidden`, symfony `keep`, laravel `forbidden` · covers `no_superfluous_phpdoc_tags`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.Commenting.UselessFunctionDocComment`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.TypeHints.ParameterTypeHint`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.TypeHints.PropertyTypeHint`, `SlevomatCodingStandard.TypeHints.ReturnTypeHint` .[decision-facts]
